  "pr_number": 3891,
  "issue_number": 3494,
  "issue_title": "Add a developer settings page for self-service webhook subscription management",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\n`POST/GET/DELETE /api/v1/webhooks/subscriptions` is API-only today with no management UI (confirmed in `workers/api.mjs`'s `handleWebhookRequest`, `src/webhooks.mjs`, `tests/webhooks-worker.test.mjs`). There is no list-all route \u2014 a caller creates a subscription (`POST /api/v1/webhooks/subscriptions`, which returns the `id` + a one-time `secret` + `filters`), then must hold onto that `id`/`secret` client-side to `GET` or `DELETE` `/api/v1/webhooks/subscriptions/{id}` later. `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/settings-popover.tsx` exists but is a display-preferences popover (theme/density/health-color palette) \u2014 there is no developer/API settings surface, and no route under `apps/ui/src/routes/` for one.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd a `/settings` (or similarly-named) developer settings page that lets a visitor create a webhook subscription, paste in an existing subscription id to check its status/delivery health, and delete a subscription they hold the secret for \u2014 entirely client-side against the public subscription-management API, no server-side UI account model.\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoints:\n  - `POST /api/v1/webhooks/subscriptions` \u2014 create. Body: `{ url, filters?: { netuids?, kinds? }, secret? }`. Response (201): `{ id, url, filters, secret, active, created_at, delivery: {...} }` \u2014 **the `secret` is returned once here and never echoed back by GET.**\n  - `GET /api/v1/webhooks/subscriptions/{id}` \u2014 read. Returns `publicSubscriptionView` (`id, url, filters, created_at, active` \u2014 no secret) plus a `delivery` health summary (`status: \"ok\"|\"retrying\"|\"dead_letter\"`, `pending`, `dead_letter`, `last_failure`).\n  - `DELETE /api/v1/webhooks/subscriptions/{id}` \u2014 requires the matching secret (see `tests/webhooks-worker.test.mjs:347` \"DELETE requires the matching secret\" \u2014 confirm the exact required header/body shape by reading `deleteWebhookSubscription` in `workers/api.mjs` before wiring it).\n  - Note: `POST` additionally requires a `METAGRAPH_WEBHOOK_SUBSCRIPTION_TOKEN`-gated header (`validateWebhookSubscriptionToken` in `workers/api.mjs:3585`) \u2014 confirm at implementation time whether that token is meant to be end-user-supplied in this UI (e.g. a field the visitor pastes in, analogous to the secret) or whether creation should be left to return a clear \"ask an operator\" error when unauthorized. Do not hardcode or bundle the token client-side.\n- Query function: **none exists.** `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` (5,044 lines) contains dozens of `queryOptions(...)` + `apiFetch<...>(...)` GET wrappers but zero webhook-related entries and zero mutations of any kind \u2014 it is a read-only data layer by convention. The one existing UI mutation precedent is `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/verify-surface-button.tsx`, which calls `useMutation({ mutationFn: async () => { const res = await apiFetch<T>(path); return res.data; } })` directly against `apiFetch` from `@/lib/metagraphed/client.ts`, **bypassing queries.ts entirely** \u2014 `apiFetch<T>(path, { init })` (see `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/client.ts:72`) forwards `opts.init` straight into the underlying `fetch`, so `method: \"POST\"`/`\"DELETE\"` + `headers`/`body` pass through unmodified.\n  - **This PR must add three `useMutation`/`apiFetch` call sites (or a small colocated hook) for create / get-by-id / delete, following the `verify-surface-button.tsx` idiom, in the new settings page or a component it owns** \u2014 plus the UI wiring to render them. A data-layer-only PR (or a UI-only PR that stubs the network calls) is exactly the failure mode this rewrite exists to prevent.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File(s) to change: new `apps/ui/src/routes/settings.tsx` (`createFileRoute(\"/settings\")`, matching the pattern in `apps/ui/src/routes/endpoints.tsx:81`), plus a new component such as `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/webhook-subscription-manager.tsx` for the create/lookup/delete forms and result rendering (keep the route file thin and put the interactive logic in the component, matching how `endpoints.tsx` delegates to `ProxyHero`/`ProxyUsagePanel`/etc.).\n- Exact anchor: nothing to extend \u2014 this is a new route. Wire it into the nav alongside the existing top-level links in `apps/ui/src/routes/__root.tsx` (see the `to=\"/\"`, `to=\"/subnets\"`, `to=\"/providers\"`, `to=\"/health\"` `Link` entries around lines 173-191) so the page is discoverable, and add a corresponding entry point (e.g. a gear/settings icon or text link) near the existing `SettingsPopover` trigger if that reads more naturally as \"Developer settings\" vs. the display-preferences popover \u2014 pick whichever placement avoids user confusion between the two \"settings\" surfaces.\n- What to render: three self-contained sections, each a form + result panel (no shared StatTile/leaderboard idiom applies here \u2014 this is form-driven, not a data table):\n  1. **Create subscription** \u2014 form fields for `url` (required, https), optional `filters.netuids` (comma-separated ints) and `filters.kinds` (checkboxes: `subnets`, `artifacts`), optional `secret`. On success, render the returned `id` and `secret` prominently with copy-to-clipboard and an explicit one-time-only warning (it will never be shown again), plus the `delivery` block (signature header name, algorithm, idempotency header) so the visitor knows how to verify incoming webhooks.\n  2. **Look up subscription** \u2014 an id input that `GET`s `/api/v1/webhooks/subscriptions/{id}` and renders `url`, `filters`, `active`, `created_at`, and the delivery-health summary (`status`, `pending`, `dead_letter`, `last_failure` when present).\n  3. **Delete subscription** \u2014 id + secret inputs that `DELETE` `/api/v1/webhooks/subscriptions/{id}` and render a confirmation or the API's rejection reason (e.g. secret mismatch, not-found).\n- Coordination note: none \u2014 no sibling issue in this tracker touches webhook subscriptions or this route; it does not overlap #3492 (Q&A box) or #3493 (semantic search omnibox), the other two AI-native/account-depth items filed alongside it in #2542.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches at least one file under `apps/ui/src/routes/` (new `settings.tsx`) and at least one file under `apps/ui/src/components/` (the manager component) \u2014 not just `queries.ts`/`types.ts`\n- [ ] The component calls `apiFetch` (directly or via a small hook) for all three operations \u2014 create (`POST`), lookup (`GET` by id), delete (`DELETE` by id) \u2014 each wired through `useMutation`/`useQuery` per the `verify-surface-button.tsx` precedent, not left as TODO stubs\n- [ ] On successful create, the response's `id` and `secret` are both rendered on-screen (with a one-time-only warning), not just logged or discarded\n- [ ] Lookup renders the delivery-health `status` (`ok`/`retrying`/`dead_letter`) distinctly, not just the raw JSON\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states are handled for each of the three operations, matching the existing convention in the codebase (`Skeleton` from `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/states.tsx` for in-flight, `EmptyState` from that same file or `RegistryEmpty` from `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/states/registry-empty.tsx` for no-result-yet, and a rendered error message \u2014 e.g. the `mutation.isError` branch pattern in `verify-surface-button.tsx` \u2014 for failures, including a distinguishable message for a 401/503 create rejection vs. a 404 lookup vs. a secret-mismatch delete)\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No subscription list/index view \u2014 the backend has no GET-all route, so this page cannot show \"all your subscriptions\"; it is strictly create/lookup-by-id/delete-by-id\n- No persistence of the id/secret in browser storage on this pass (e.g. localStorage \"remember my subscriptions\") \u2014 that's a separate enhancement, not required for this issue\n- No changes to `src/webhooks.mjs` or `workers/api.mjs` \u2014 the backend routes are already shipped; this issue is UI-only\n- Do not duplicate or touch #3492 (Q&A box) or #3493 (semantic search omnibox) work in the same file\n\n## Size\n\nSize: M \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
